anv/measure: initialize the batch's list link in anv_measure_init()

anv_measure_reset() calls anv_measure_init() for a command buffer that has no measure batch yet (capture was off when it
was allocated, e.g. INTEL_MEASURE=...,start=N) and returns right away, so the batch keeps the zeroed link vk_alloc +
memset left. Its first submission with snapshots then dereferences measure->base.link.next (NULL) in
_anv_measure_submit()'s "reused command buffer without reset" check (0eed818588a): Minecraft 26.3 (Vulkan) died with
SIGSEGV in _anv_measure_submit+0x50 from xe_queue_exec_locked the moment capture started at frame 20000. Platform
independent; upstream main has the same code. Also leave cmd_buffer->measure NULL when the allocation fails instead of
writing through a NULL pointer.

--- a/src/intel/vulkan/anv_measure.c
+++ b/src/intel/vulkan/anv_measure.c
@@ -85,8 +85,19 @@
       vk_alloc(&cmd_buffer->vk.pool->alloc,
                batch_bytes, 8,
                VK_SYSTEM_ALLOCATION_SCOPE_OBJECT);
+   if (measure == NULL) {
+      cmd_buffer->measure = NULL;
+      return;
+   }
 
    memset(measure, 0, batch_bytes);
+   /* _anv_measure_submit() looks at the link to spot a command buffer
+    * submitted again without a reset. anv_measure_reset() sets it up, but a
+    * command buffer allocated while capture was off (INTEL_MEASURE start=N)
+    * gets here from anv_measure_reset(), which returns before doing so: a
+    * zeroed link made the first submission with snapshots dereference NULL.
+    */
+   list_inithead(&measure->base.link);
    cmd_buffer->measure = measure;
    if(config->cpu_measure)
       return;
